The Germans generally speak of ♭ and ♯ as Be, Kreuz (cross). I do not remember ever having heard the ♮ named, but I find in Flügel's Dictionary *Bequadratum* (square b) and *Wiederherstellungszeichen* (sign of restitution, for which ♮ was not used till the seventeenth century). ANCHOR
>>>
